title The banner and the path compared by a meter, and a bound guard four laps unrun
prompt Take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds, read one council-rota row, send the increment.
think Read KYRI.md and RADIANT_STYLE.md first, then crux/REMEMBER.md, then the top three rows of session-logs/README.md with their recommend lines. The running thread is the Caravan ladder lift arc; the newest recommend named a companion question rather than a rung -- a meter that reports when a living document's own Status and room banner last agreed with where the file actually sits.
think Council rota row 4 -- Earth/Mercury, the concrete: the one-clock naming law, TWO_ROOMS, the marked value. The row handed the crux directly. foundations/20260703-202312_the-marked-value.md opened with **Register:** active-designing while living in foundations/, which is the third file of that exact shape in three laps.
think Standfast first: crux/REDS.md read closed through %147, so no open agent-closable red stood in the way of new work. The banner drift was then booked as %148 and closed in the same round, which is reds-first working rather than reds-first skipped.
think Designed the check narrow on measurement rather than on intuition. Surveyed the whole tree first: Register/Room/Shelf fields whose first word is a shelf this tree files on number 29, of which 26 agreed and 3 drifted, with zero false positives. Including **Status:** in the same rule would have caught three honest lines -- Status: Counsel, Status: Gratitude -- because Status says what a piece IS rather than where it lives, so Status is deliberately free and the exemption is proven in the control rather than asserted in a comment.
think Wrote tools/fixtures/banner_room_scan.sh, then repointed the three drifted lines to name foundations and record the 20260821.211423 graduation as landed rather than still pending, then tools/fixtures/banner_room_control.sh with four planted documents covering both verdicts and both exemptions, then tools/banner_room_witness.rish. Gate at zero with no slack, since the field is at zero.
think Ran the cold-start roster afterward rather than trusting it, which is the roster's own sentence. tools/gen/season/equinox_e123_living_pin_guard_witness.rish went RED: crux/REDS.md stood at 26,626 bytes against a 24,576-byte bound, over it before this lap wrote a byte, across four laps that each booked a row and none ran the guard. Booked as %149.
think Reading the fold pointers to place the new fold found a second miss of the same shape: rows %142-%143 had folded to crux/archive/ on 20260822.194931 with the archive file committed and the doorway line pointing at it never written into the living pin, so one range of the ledger was safe on disk and unreachable from the only page that says where ranges go.
think Folded rows %144 through %147 to two new archive files, wrote the missing %142-%143 doorway line, and carried the pin to 20,331 bytes. The reds-monotone witness refused twice on the way -- first the headline total, then the span -- each time because a number was one row behind the spine, which is the guard doing exactly its job.
obs The finding worth carrying is that a header field naming a shelf is a claim about the filesystem, checkable the same way a digest is, and both halves were already on disk -- the field in the header, the directory in the path -- with nothing standing between them. Three consecutive laps caught one apiece by hand, which is the definition of a lantern; the third became a loom.
obs The narrowness is the design, and it is proven rather than asserted. A scan that refused **Register:** Checkable or **Status:** Counsel would red on most of the tree's own headers, and a witness the bench routes around is worse than none, so the control plants both exemptions and proves they pass free.
obs The fold is two acts rather than one -- moving the bytes, and repointing the page that leads to them -- and only the first is visible in a diff that looks finished. That is why rows %142-%143 lost their doorway for four laps with every guard green.
obs The dated-path census read the control's four planted throwaway filenames as real broken references, raising refs_lost from 192 to 196. The honest repair is the single exclusion list both dated-path tools read, not a raised ceiling: banner_room_control.sh joins room_bound_control.sh and shipped_binary_claim_control.sh as instrument rather than field, and the census returned to the exact 192 baseline.
obs Folding rows to crux/archive/ moves them one directory deeper, so their relative links needed repointing from ../tools/ to ../../tools/. Every link in both new archive files was checked to resolve on disk before the fold was believed. The elder archives carry the same one-level-off pattern and are left for their own touch rather than swept here.
obs No .rye moved this lap, so the Caravan choir was not run; the ladder arc's queue is unchanged and named in REMEMBER for the next lap.
loom witness=banner_room banners_naming_a_shelf=29 agreeing=29 drifted=0 ceiling=0
loom scan=dated_path_census refs_lost=192 lost_ceiling=192 under_ceiling=yes
loom pin=crux/REDS.md bytes_before=26626 bytes_after=20331 bound=24576 rows_folded=4 doorway_lines=19
file tools/fixtures/banner_room_scan.sh the meter -- first word of a Register/Room/Shelf banner must be a directory the file sits in
file tools/fixtures/banner_room_control.sh both verdicts and both exemptions proven on a throwaway repository
file tools/banner_room_witness.rish the rung -- field at zero drifted, control agreeing with itself
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_exclusions.sh the control's planted fixtures named as instrument rather than field, on the one list both tools read
file foundations/20260703-200712_what-needs-ordering.md Register repointed to foundations, graduation named as landed
file foundations/20260703-201612_the-sealed-crossing.md Register repointed to foundations, graduation named as landed
file foundations/20260703-202312_the-marked-value.md Register repointed to foundations, graduation named as landed
file crux/REDS.md rows %148 and %149 booked and closed, rows %144-%147 folded, the missing %142-%143 doorway written, headline and span refreshed to the measured spine
file crux/archive/REDS-keyword-in-the-key-and-the-unranked-queue-rows-144-145.md the fold, every byte kept, links repointed for the new depth
file crux/archive/REDS-the-unpriced-queue-and-eight-drifting-guards-rows-146-147.md the fold, every byte kept, links repointed for the new depth
file crux/REMEMBER.md Now refilled with this lap, prior edge condensed to one clause, banner_room seated on the standing-equipment roster
recommend keep-going the ladder arc's queue is unchanged and waiting -- rests_path leads the free-absolutely reading at 250 over eleven rungs, confer_words holds the queue's free head at 294 over forty-three rungs priced at forty-three import re-exports, and answered_by still leads by return at 330 costing sixty-eight openings. Beside it, two rounds running have now found standing equipment behind the code it guards, so the question REDS %147 opened is sharper rather than answered: a meter that reports when each guard last ran would have caught the living-pin bound on the lap it crossed rather than four laps later.
